Regina OO workspace session. )HELP lists the commands, )OFF ends it.
      )SAVE [wsid]          save the workspace in wsid.rxws
)LOAD wsid            clear, then load wsid.rxws
)OUT file [names]     write all or some names to file.rxo
)IN file [names]      read all or some names from a file
)VARS )FNS )CLASSES   list variables, routines, classes
)ERASE names          erase variables, routines, classes
)SHOW name            show the source of a routine or class
)WSID [name]          show or set the workspace name
)CLEAR                empty workspace
)GC                   collect unused objects now
)OFF                  end the session
A line with an expression shows its value. Lines that start
with :: define routines and classes, up to an empty line.
            42
            a-b
      a literal is shown too
          :     :     : HYP
      25
          :     :     :     :     :     :     :     : COUNTER
            1 2
      C X Y
      HYP
      COUNTER
      WAS CLEAR WS
      SAVED sessiontest.rxws
      CLEAR WS
      
      LOADED sessiontest
      42 b 169 3
            set
      4
      3
      3
            ::routine hyp
  use arg a, b
  return a * a + b * b

            C M Y
      Error 42.3: Arithmetic overflow; divisor must not be zero
      after the error
      WRITTEN sessionpart.rxo
      CLEAR WS
      Y
      Y
            rc=0
